    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALESMAN",
      "quote": "I bought him every kind of remedy,\n                           out of my own pocket. Nothing\n                           palliated. Although one of them he\n                           drank avidly. And it was an\n                           extremely rattly cough. No, I was\n                           not sad to see Mr. Kincaid leave.",
      "block": 92
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p12",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LANDLADY",
      "quote": "It was not a contagious cough.\n                           Nobody here became ill. It was a\n                           nervous cough. I would not rent to\n                           a contagious cougher.",
      "block": 93
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALESMAN",
      "quote": "I have never heard of a nervous\n                         cough.\n                               (turns to Mrs. Longabaugh)\n                         I understand you are about to leave\n                         us.",
      "block": 94
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p12",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LANDLADY",
      "quote": "There is no medical affliction but\n                         that doesn’t have a nervous\n                         variety. The nervous system spreads\n                         its tendrils throughout the body. I\n                         saw a picture of it in a book.",
      "block": 95
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALESMAN",
      "quote": "The nervous system does not have\n                         “tendrils.”",
      "block": 96
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p12",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LANDLADY",
      "quote": "I don’t pretend to be a physician,\n                         or a botanist. I know that the\n                         nervous system extends through the\n                         body and I presume that that is how\n                         it learns of the various physical\n                         conditions that it imitates.",
      "block": 97
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p13",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ANOTHER MAN",
      "quote": "Mrs. Flannery is quite right, I\n                         have seen that picture.",
      "block": 98
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p12",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LANDLADY",
      "quote": "My point is only that Mr. Kincaid\n                         was not a contagious cougher. I\n                         don’t rent to such.",
      "block": 99
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p14",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MIDDLE-AGED WOMAN",
      "quote": "Is there any more chicken and\n                         dumplings? The bowl came to me\n                         last.",
      "block": 100
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p12",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LANDLADY",
      "quote": "Yes there is more! We don’t stint\n                         at this table. Grandma Turner looks\n                         to be finished. Are you finished\n                         Grandma Turner!",
      "block": 101
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p12",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LANDLADY (CONT’D)",
      "quote": "... Grandma Turner is finished.",
      "block": 102
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALESMAN (to Alice)",
      "quote": "(to Alice)\n                         Leaving tomorrow? Jumping off the\n                         map, so to speak?",
      "block": 103
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "Yes indeed, my brother and I are\n                         setting off in the morning, for\n                         Oregon.",
      "block": 104
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALESMAN",
      "quote": "Oregon! You have people there, or\n                         a—",
      "block": 105
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p12",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LANDLADY",
      "quote": "Just scoop from her plate, Mrs.\n                         Halliday. Grandma Turner is quite\n                         done.",
      "block": 106
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "No, I, not exactly—that is, my\n                         brother does.",
      "block": 107
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p16",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "GILBERT",
      "quote": "Well go ahead and tell him Alice,\n                         don’t be tongue-tied. She has\n                         exciting news.",
      "block": 108
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "I’m... I’m to be married. Or at\n                         least I may be, to Gilbert’s...\n                         associate.",
      "block": 109
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p16",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "GILBERT",
      "quote": "He’s well fixed out there.",
      "block": 110
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALESMAN",
      "quote": "You’re not certain whether you’re\n                         going to be married? Has the\n                         gentleman not proposed?",
      "block": 111
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "Well, he—",
      "block": 112
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p16",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "GILBERT",
      "quote": "He will propose. Once they meet\n                          each other I’m sure Alice will pass",
      "block": 113
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "Uh huh.",
      "block": 114
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "Yes, it uh... Of course you will do\n                         fine, solo, no doubt about it, a\n                         man of your skills will always be\n                         in high demand.",
      "block": 115
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "... Wheres’at mecate rope?—Neb\n                         mind, here it is.",
      "block": 116
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "... When will we see buffalo?",
      "block": 117
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "Oh soon, very soon.",
      "block": 118
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "... Used to hunt the big shaggies,\n                         provisioned for the army. Did some\n                         trapping. Years. Found myself\n                         missing animals’t walked upright.\n                         Started piloting. Partnered up with\n                         Mr. Arthur.",
      "block": 119
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "What did Mr. Arthur do, previously?",
      "block": 120
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "Don’t know...",
      "block": 121
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "... That man is a wonder. He can\n                         read the prairie like a book. To\n                         see him cut for sign, well—you’d\n                         think the good lord dealt us each\n                         our five senses, then bottom-dealt\n                         Mr. Arthur one extra. Still... he\n                         is old. I don’t know how it will go\n                         with him. His affairs may... I\n                         can’t help feeling in the wrong.",
      "block": 122
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "Your first responsibility is to\n         your household.",
      "block": 123
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "Yes, but...",
      "block": 124
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "I’m sorry. I should not dismiss it\n         with an easy apothegm.",
      "block": 125
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "Yes.",
      "block": 126
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "Yes.",
      "block": 127
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "Gilbert had a saying for any\n         situation. A ready bit of wisdom.\n         He was very certain.",
      "block": 128
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "He was a doughface?",
      "block": 129
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "How did—oh, yes. He was an admirer\n         of President Pierce, yes, very much\n         so. He had fixed political beliefs.\n         All of his beliefs were quite\n         fixed, even those that... fortune\n         did not tend to endorse. He would\n         upbraid me for being “wishy-washy.”\n         I never had his certainties. I\n         suppose it’s a defect.",
      "block": 130
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "Oh, I don’t think it is a defect at\n         all. Oh no. Uncertainty—that is\n         appropriate for the matters of this\n         world. Only regarding the next are\n         we vouchsafed certainty.",
      "block": 131
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p15",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ALICE",
      "quote": "Strait is the gate...",
      "block": 132
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p18",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "BILLY KNAPP",
      "quote": "... and narrow the way. Indeed.\n                          Indeed.",
      "block": 133
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p8",
      "to": "p17",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MAN",
      "quote": "Sign, Mr. Arthur?",
      "block": 134
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "Horses.\n                               (a gesture forward as he mounts up)\n                          Keep on. Gonna talk to Mr. Knapp.",
      "block": 135
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "Wharza woman?",
      "block": 136
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p19",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MATT",
      "quote": "Tsat?",
      "block": 137
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "Mrs. Longabaugh, wharshe?",
      "block": 138
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p19",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MATT",
      "quote": "Went o’er air.",
      "block": 139
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "O’er air? Whyzat?",
      "block": 140
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p19",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MATT",
      "quote": "Huh. I’dno. Heard that mutt\n                         barkin’. Pres’dent Pierce.",
      "block": 141
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "Whenshe go?",
      "block": 142
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p19",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MATT",
      "quote": "Wull. I’dno.",
      "block": 143
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "Whenshe go?!",
      "block": 144
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p19",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MATT",
      "quote": "Half ar.",
      "block": 145
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p17",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "MR. ARTHUR",
      "quote": "Uh-hnghh.",
      "block": 146
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p20",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "TRAPPER",
      "quote": "You did not wake me!",
      "block": 147
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p20",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "TRAPPER (CONT’D)",
      "quote": "... For I was not asleep.",
      "block": 148
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p21",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "THIGPEN",
      "quote": "Oh, not asleep, I see.",
      "block": 149
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p20",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "TRAPPER",
      "quote": "How much to go d’you reckon?",
      "block": 150
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p20",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "TRAPPER",
      "quote": "Me? No. You?",
      "block": 151
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p20",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "TRAPPER",
      "quote": "Him’s yourn?",
      "block": 152
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p22",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "LADY",
      "quote": "A loved one?",
      "block": 153
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p21",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "THIGPEN (giggle)",
      "quote": "By somebody, perhaps!",
      "block": 154
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p23",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "FRENCHMAN",
      "quote": "You did not know heem?",
      "block": 155
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p21",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "THIGPEN (giggle)",
      "quote": "We knew him only at the end.",
      "block": 156
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p24",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "CLARENCE",
      "quote": "At the very end.",
      "block": 157
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p20",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "TRAPPER",
      "quote": "No!",
      "block": 158
    },
    {
